Convert one container block into another by moving its cells across AND cascade-converting each to a type the target region allows, and convert a single-value block to/from a container region. Container conversion runs in the new pathMap-aware `reshapeContainerBlock` (the path `convertBlockInPlace` takes for a block with children): it moves regions via `convertContainerBlock`, then converts any cell whose type isn't in the target region's addable set — resolved through `addableSiblingTypes` with the live `blockPathMap` `descendantDisallowedTypes`, each cell reaching the first allowed type its own `fieldMappings` can (transitively). value↔region uses the shared `expandValueIntoRegion`/`collapseRegionToValue` helpers (expand for a childless value source in `convertBlockType`; collapse for a container source in `reshapeContainerBlock`). This makes e.g. tabs⇄steps⇄definitionList and value⇄container conversions work from "Convert to…", cells and content preserved. (Nested `data/items` regions — accordion — are a follow-up: `getContainerRegionDescriptors` surfaces only top-level regions.)
